<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · North America and Oceania</p><h1 class="st-title">Chiefdom of Oahu</h1><p class="st-meta">1400 CE – 1795 CE (approx.) · capital Waikiki</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Hawaiian chiefdom of Oʻahu, centred on Waikīkī, whose conquest by Kamehameha I at the Battle of Nuʻuanu in 1795 created the Kingdom of Hawaii.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oahu">Oʻahu's</a> districts were drawn under a single ruling line by around 1400. Tradition remembers the 16th-century aliʻi nui <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kakuhihewa">Kākuhihewa</a> as presiding over a peaceful, prosperous island, and chiefly residences clustered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waikiki">Waikīkī</a>, with its fishponds and coconut groves, and at sacred sites such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kukaniloko">Kūkaniloko</a>, the royal birthplace in central Oʻahu.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The aliʻi nui ruled through priests, district chiefs and the kapu system, and the island's fertile valleys supported intensive taro terraces and large fishponds. In 1773 the chiefs chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kahahana">Kahahana</a> as ruler, but in 1783 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kahekili-ii">Kahekili II</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chiefdom-of-maui">Chiefdom of Maui</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oahu">Oʻahu</a> and ruled it until his death in 1794. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalanikupule">Kalanikūpule</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaeokulani">Kaʻeokulani</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kauai">Kauaʻi</a> that year with the help of the British trader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-brown-sea-captain">William Brown</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1795 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamehameha-i">Kamehameha I</a> landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waikiki">Waikīkī</a> and defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalanikupule">Kalanikūpule</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nuuanu">Battle of Nuʻuanu</a>, where many defenders were driven over the Pali cliffs. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oahu">Oʻahu</a> became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-hawaii">Kingdom of Hawaii</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honolulu">Honolulu</a> later grew into its capital.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1400 CE – 1795 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">North America and Oceania</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:87.56%;width:7.86%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1400 CE – 1795 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Waikiki</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kākuhihewa, Kahahana, Kalanikūpule</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hawaiian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hawaiian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-states">United States</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Oʻahu</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1598&amp;focus=chiefdom-of-oahu" aria-label="Chiefdom of Oahu on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2279 769 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Chiefdom of Oahu lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M790 1661h0M759 1646h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2599 1025h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M2599 1025h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United States. <a href="/atlas?year=1598&amp;focus=chiefdom-of-oahu">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

